IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja1-part3-div2-jurisdiction.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- LAYER 1, Part 3, Division 2 "Original jurisdiction": ss 15, 16, 17 and 17A (criminal and civil jurisdiction; the Syariah Court carve-out). The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` only. The Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966, the Women's Charter 1961, the Mediation Act 2017,
-- the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020 and the other Acts these sections cite are not among the sources: what they decide is asked as a fact.

§ `Part 3: General Division of High Court (continued)`

§§ `Division 2: Original jurisdiction`

§§§ `Section 15: Criminal jurisdiction`

-- The facts s 15(1) turns on, one field per paragraph. A field is TRUE if that paragraph's circumstance is present.
DECLARE `s 15(1) offence` HAS
    `committed within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed on board a ship or aircraft registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed on the high seas or on an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `piracy by the law of nations committed on the high seas` IS A BOOLEAN
    `punishable under the Hijacking of Aircraft and Protection of Aircraft and International Airports Act 1978 or the Maritime Offences Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a written law provides that it is triable in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 15(1). Plain gloss: does the General Division have jurisdiction to try this offence? Paragraphs (a) to (f); (c) needs the offender to be a citizen of Singapore. The list does not say "only".
-- src:994 | 15.—(1) The General Division has jurisdiction to try all offences
-- src:995 | committed —
-- src:997 | (a) within Singapore;
-- src:999 | (b) on board any ship or aircraft registered in Singapore;
-- src:1001 | (c) by any person who is a citizen of Singapore on the high
-- src:1002 | seas or on any aircraft;
-- src:1004 | (d) by any person on the high seas where the offence is piracy
-- src:1005 | by the law of nations;
-- src:1007 | (e) by any person within or outside Singapore where the
-- src:1008 | offence is punishable under and by virtue of the provisions
-- src:1009 | of the Hijacking of Aircraft and Protection of Aircraft and
-- src:1010 | International Airports Act 1978 or the Maritime Offences
-- src:1011 | Act 2003; and
-- src:1013 | (f) in any place or by any person if it is provided in any written
-- src:1014 | law that the offence is triable in Singapore.
@ref s 15(1) (src:994-1014)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 15(1) offence`
      offender IS A Person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(1) the General Division has jurisdiction to try the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF offence's `committed within Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        IF offence's `committed on board a ship or aircraft registered in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        IF offender's `is a citizen of Singapore` AND offence's `committed on the high seas or on an aircraft` THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
        IF offence's `piracy by the law of nations committed on the high seas` THEN JUST TRUE -- (d)
        IF offence's `punishable under the Hijacking of Aircraft and Protection of Aircraft and International Airports Act 1978 or the Maritime Offences Act 2003` THEN JUST TRUE -- (e)
        IF offence's `a written law provides that it is triable in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE -- (f)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "has jurisdiction to try all offences committed" (a) to (f), with no "only"

-- s 15(2). The General Division may pass any sentence allowed by law.
-- src:1018 | (2) The General Division may pass any sentence allowed by law.
@ref s 15(2) (src:1018)
GIVEN `the sentence is allowed by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence one that the law allows for the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the General Division may pass the sentence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sentence is allowed by law` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any sentence allowed by law"

§§§ `Section 16: Civil jurisdiction -- general`

-- s 16(1). Plain gloss: does the General Division have jurisdiction to hear and try this action in personam? Where the defendant is served (in Singapore, or outside it as the Rules authorise) with an
-- originating claim or other originating process, or submits to the General Division's jurisdiction. "where" that is not met is a no for this subsection (ruling of 2026-11-05); s 16(2) and s 17 are other routes.
-- src:1029 | 16.—(1) The General Division has jurisdiction to hear and try any
-- src:1030 | action in personam where —
-- src:1032 | (a) the defendant is served with an originating claim or any
-- src:1033 | other originating process —
-- src:1035 | (i) in Singapore in the manner prescribed by Rules of
-- src:1036 | Court or Family Justice Rules; or
-- src:1038 | (ii) outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by
-- src:1039 | and in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court or
-- src:1040 | Family Justice Rules; or
-- src:1044 | (b) the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the General
-- src:1045 | Division.
@ref s 16(1) (src:1029-1045)
GIVEN `the action is an action in personam` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action one in personam (against a person, rather than against property)?
      `the defendant is served in Singapore in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant served with the originating claim or other originating process in Singapore, in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules?
      `the defendant is served outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant served outside Singapore, in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules?
      `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the defendant submit to the jurisdiction of the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the General Division has jurisdiction to hear and try the action in personam` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is an action in personam` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any action in personam"
        IF `the defendant is served in Singapore in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)(i)
        IF `the defendant is served outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)(ii)
        IF `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the General Division` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where (a) the defendant is served ... or (b) the defendant submits to the jurisdiction"

-- s 16(2). Without limiting (1), the General Division has such jurisdiction as any other written law vests in it.
-- src:1049 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the General Division has such
-- src:1050 | jurisdiction as is vested in it by any other written law.
@ref s 16(2) (src:1049-1050)
GIVEN `another written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another written law vest the jurisdiction in the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2) the General Division has the jurisdiction vested in it by another written law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `another written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such jurisdiction as is vested in it by any other written law"

§§§ `Section 17: Civil jurisdiction -- specific`

-- s 17(1). Plain gloss: is this subject within the civil jurisdiction of the General Division that s 17(1) names? "Without limiting section 16 ... includes": the eight paragraphs are named,
-- the list is open. (g) is limited to a dispute "for which no proceedings have been commenced in a court".
-- src:1056 | 17.—(1) Without limiting section 16, the civil jurisdiction of the
-- src:1057 | General Division includes —
-- src:1059 | (a) jurisdiction under any written law relating to divorce and
-- src:1060 | matrimonial causes;
-- src:1062 | (b) jurisdiction under any written law relating to matters of
-- src:1063 | admiralty;
-- src:1065 | (c) jurisdiction under any written law relating to bankruptcy or
-- src:1066 | to companies;
-- src:1068 | (d) jurisdiction to appoint and control guardians of infants and
-- src:1069 | generally over the persons and property of infants;
-- src:1071 | (e) jurisdiction to appoint and control guardians and keepers
-- src:1072 | of the persons and estates of idiots, mentally disordered
-- src:1073 | persons and persons of unsound mind;
-- src:1080 | (f) jurisdiction to grant probates of wills and testaments,
-- src:1081 | letters of administration of the estates of deceased persons
-- src:1082 | and to alter or revoke such grants;
-- src:1084 | (g) jurisdiction under the Mediation Act 2017 to record a
-- src:1085 | mediated settlement agreement made in a mediation, in
-- src:1086 | relation to a dispute for which no proceedings have been
-- src:1087 | commenced in a court, as an order of court; and
-- src:1089 | (h) jurisdiction under the Singapore Convention on Mediation
-- src:1090 | Act 2020 to grant the applications provided for in that Act
-- src:1091 | in respect of international settlement agreements.
@ref s 17(1) (src:1056-1091)
GIVEN subject IS A `Subject of the case` @desc What is the case about (divorce, admiralty, bankruptcy, companies, guardianship of infants, guardianship of persons of unsound mind, probate or administration, a mediated settlement agreement to be recorded, an international settlement agreement, or something else)?
      `no proceedings have been commenced in a court for the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a mediated settlement agreement: have no proceedings been commenced in a court for the dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) the civil jurisdiction of the General Division includes the subject` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `divorce and matrimonial causes` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
    WHEN `admiralty or shipping` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
    WHEN bankruptcy THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
    WHEN companies THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
    WHEN `guardianship of infants` THEN JUST TRUE -- (d)
    WHEN `guardianship of mentally disordered persons or persons of unsound mind` THEN JUST TRUE -- (e)
    WHEN `probate or letters of administration` THEN JUST TRUE -- (f)
    WHEN `recording a mediated settlement agreement under the Mediation Act 2017` THEN
        IF `no proceedings have been commenced in a court for the dispute` THEN JUST TRUE -- (g)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a dispute for which no proceedings have been commenced in a court"
    WHEN `an international settlement agreement under the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` THEN JUST TRUE -- (h)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the civil jurisdiction of the General Division includes"

-- s 17(2). Three terms with the meanings other Acts give them: the answer is the borrowed fact the person states.
-- src:1095 | (2) In this section —
-- src:1097 | “international settlement agreement” has the meaning given by
-- src:1098 | section 2(1) of the Singapore Convention on Mediation
-- src:1099 | Act 2020;
@ref s 17(2) “international settlement agreement” (src:1095-1099)
GIVEN `it is an international settlement agreement within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an international settlement agreement within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) international settlement agreement: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` MEANS
    JUST `it is an international settlement agreement within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020`

-- src:1101 | “mediated settlement agreement” and “mediation” have the
-- src:1102 | meanings given by the Mediation Act 2017.
@ref s 17(2) “mediated settlement agreement” and “mediation” (src:1101-1102)
GIVEN `it is a mediated settlement agreement within the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a mediated settlement agreement within the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) mediated settlement agreement: it has the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017` MEANS
    JUST `it is a mediated settlement agreement within the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017`

@ref s 17(2) “mediation” (src:1101-1102)
GIVEN `it is a mediation within the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a mediation within the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) mediation: it has the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017` MEANS
    JUST `it is a mediation within the meaning given by the Mediation Act 2017`

§§§ `Section 17A: Concurrent jurisdiction with the Syariah Court in certain matters`

-- A set of civil proceedings in the General Division, with the facts s 17A(1) to (6) turn on.
DECLARE `s 17A civil proceedings` HAS
    matter IS A `Subject of the case`
    `all the parties are Muslims` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties were married under the Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `commenced in the General Division on` IS A DATE
    `divorce proceedings commenced in the Syariah Court on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `decree or order for divorce made by the Syariah Court on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `divorce registered under section 102 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `a Syariah Court commencement certificate has been filed with the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Syariah Court continuation certificate has been filed with the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
    `commenced by consent of the parties with the certificates of attendance filed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `continued by consent of the parties with the certificates of attendance filed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 17A(1). Despite ss 16 and 17, the General Division has NO jurisdiction to hear civil proceedings involving matters within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under s 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the
-- Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 in which all the parties are Muslims or the parties were married under the Muslim law. JUST TRUE here means "has no jurisdiction".
-- src:1109 | 17A.—(1) Despite sections 16 and 17, the General Division has no
-- src:1110 | jurisdiction to hear and try any civil proceedings involving matters
-- src:1111 | which come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under
-- src:1112 | section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law
-- src:1113 | Act 1966 in which all the parties are Muslims or where the parties
-- src:1114 | were married under the provisions of the Muslim law.
@ref s 17A(1) (src:1109-1114)
GIVEN `the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
      `all the parties are Muslims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the parties Muslims?
      `the parties were married under the Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the parties married under the provisions of the Muslim law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(1) the General Division has no jurisdiction to hear and try the civil proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966`
           AND (`all the parties are Muslims` OR `the parties were married under the Muslim law`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "matters which come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) ... in which all the parties are Muslims or where the parties were married under the provisions of the Muslim law"

-- s 17A(2). Even though such matters come within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under s 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d), the General Division has the jurisdiction any written law vests in it over
-- civil proceedings about (a) maintenance for a wife or child, (b) custody of a child, (c) disposition or division of property on divorce.
-- src:1118 | (2) Even though such matters come within the jurisdiction of the
-- src:1119 | Syariah Court under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d) of
-- src:1120 | the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966, the General Division
-- src:1121 | has jurisdiction as is vested in it by any written law to hear and try any
-- src:1122 | civil proceedings involving matters relating to —
-- src:1124 | (a) maintenance for any wife or child;
-- src:1126 | (b) custody of any child; and
-- src:1133 | (c) disposition or division of property on divorce.
@ref s 17A(2) (src:1118-1133)
GIVEN subject IS A `Subject of the case` @desc What is the proceeding about: maintenance for a wife or child, custody of a child, disposition or division of property on divorce, or something else?
      `the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
      `a written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law vest the jurisdiction to hear and try the proceeding in the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(2) the General Division has the jurisdiction vested in it by written law over the civil proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (subject EQUALS `maintenance for a wife or child` OR subject EQUALS `custody of a child` OR subject EQUALS `disposition or division of property on divorce`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) maintenance for any wife or child; (b) custody of any child; and (c) disposition or division of property on divorce"
        IF NOT `the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such matters" come within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d)
        IF `a written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as is vested in it by any written law"

-- s 17A(3), (5), (6). Plain gloss: is the General Division to stay these civil proceedings? "Where" the proceedings involve a matter in s 17A(2)(b) or (c) and parties who are Muslims or were married
-- under the Muslim law, they are stayed (a) [matters (b) and (c)] if commenced on or after a Syariah Court divorce event, unless a Syariah Court commencement certificate has been filed;
-- (b) [custody only] if a divorce event follows the commencement, unless a continuation certificate has been filed. (5) and (6) switch (a) and (b) off where the proceedings were commenced / continued
-- by consent with the certificates of attendance filed. A "where" or "if" not met, an "unless" or "does not apply" met, are each the text's no (fork F8; marginal readings M2, M3).
-- src:1137 | (3) Where civil proceedings involving any matter referred to in
-- src:1138 | subsection (2)(b) or (c) and involving parties who are Muslims or
-- src:1139 | were married under the provisions of the Muslim law are commenced
-- src:1140 | in the General Division, the General Division is to stay the civil
-- src:1141 | proceedings —
-- src:1143 | (a) involving any matter referred to in subsection (2)(b) or (c),
-- src:1144 | if the civil proceedings are commenced on or after the
-- src:1145 | commencement of proceedings for divorce in the Syariah
-- src:1146 | Court or after the making of a decree or order for divorce
-- src:1147 | by the Syariah Court or on or after the registration of any
-- src:1148 | divorce under section 102 of the Administration of Muslim
-- src:1149 | Law Act 1966 between the same parties, unless a Syariah
-- src:1150 | Court commencement certificate in respect of the civil
-- src:1151 | proceedings has been filed with the General Division;
-- src:1153 | (b) involving any matter referred to in subsection (2)(b), if
-- src:1154 | proceedings for divorce are commenced in the Syariah
-- src:1155 | Court or a decree or order for divorce is made by the
-- src:1156 | Syariah Court or a divorce is registered under section 102
-- src:1157 | of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 between
-- src:1158 | the same parties after the commencement of the civil
-- src:1159 | proceedings, unless a Syariah Court continuation
-- src:1160 | certificate in respect of the civil proceedings has been
-- src:1161 | filed with the General Division.
-- src:1187 | (5) Subsection (3)(a) does not apply if the civil proceedings
-- src:1188 | referred to therein are commenced in the General Division by the
-- src:1189 | consent of the parties to the proceedings and the certificates of
-- src:1190 | attendance of the parties issued under section 35A(7) of the
-- src:1191 | Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 have been filed in
-- src:1192 | accordance with Family Justice Rules.
-- src:1196 | (6) Subsection (3)(b) does not apply if the civil proceedings
-- src:1197 | referred to therein are continued by the consent of the parties to
-- src:1198 | the proceedings and the certificates of attendance of the parties issued
-- src:1199 | under section 35A(7) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966
-- src:1200 | have been filed in accordance with Family Justice Rules.
@ref s 17A(3), (5) and (6) (src:1137-1200)
GIVEN p IS A `s 17A civil proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(3) the General Division is to stay the civil proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (p's `all the parties are Muslims` OR p's `the parties were married under the Muslim law`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where civil proceedings ... involving parties who are Muslims or were married under the provisions of the Muslim law"
        IF p's matter EQUALS `custody of a child`
           AND `s 17A(3)(a) a Syariah Court divorce event precedes or coincides with the civil proceedings` p
           AND NOT p's `a Syariah Court commencement certificate has been filed with the General Division`
           AND NOT p's `commenced by consent of the parties with the certificates of attendance filed` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a), matter (2)(b)
        IF p's matter EQUALS `disposition or division of property on divorce`
           AND `s 17A(3)(a) a Syariah Court divorce event precedes or coincides with the civil proceedings` p
           AND NOT p's `a Syariah Court commencement certificate has been filed with the General Division`
           AND NOT p's `commenced by consent of the parties with the certificates of attendance filed` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a), matter (2)(c)
        IF p's matter EQUALS `custody of a child`
           AND `s 17A(3)(b) a Syariah Court divorce event follows the commencement of the civil proceedings` p
           AND NOT p's `a Syariah Court continuation certificate has been filed with the General Division`
           AND NOT p's `continued by consent of the parties with the certificates of attendance filed` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b), matter (2)(b)
        IF NOT (p's matter EQUALS `custody of a child` OR p's matter EQUALS `disposition or division of property on divorce`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where civil proceedings involving any matter referred to in subsection (2)(b) or (c)"; maintenance for a wife or child, (2)(a), is not one (fork F8: both "where" limbs answer alike)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if" no divorce event in the Syariah Court (a) precedes the civil proceedings, or (b) follows them; "unless" a certificate has been filed; (5) and (6) "does not apply"

-- s 17A(3), paragraph (a): the Syariah Court events that make the General Division stay custody and property proceedings: divorce proceedings commenced there on or before the civil
-- proceedings' day (same day deemed before, s 17A(4)); a decree or order for divorce made there before it; or a divorce registered (before 1 March 2009, s 17A(3A)) on or before it.
@ref s 17A(3)(a) the Syariah Court events (src:1143-1151)
GIVEN p IS A `s 17A civil proceedings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17A(3)(a) a Syariah Court divorce event precedes or coincides with the civil proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `divorce proceedings commenced in the Syariah Court on`
        WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST p's `commenced in the General Division on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    OR  CONSIDER p's `decree or order for divorce made by the Syariah Court on`
        WHEN JUST d THEN d LESS THAN p's `commenced in the General Division on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    OR  CONSIDER p's `divorce registered under section 102 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 on`
        WHEN JUST d THEN `s 17A(3A) the registration of the divorce counts for section 17A(3)` d EQUALS JUST TRUE AND d AT MOST p's `commenced in the General Division on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 17A(3), paragraph (b): the same events occurring AFTER the civil proceedings were commenced (a same-day commencement is deemed before, so it is not "after").
@ref s 17A(3)(b) the Syariah Court events (src:1153-1161)
GIVEN p IS A `s 17A civil proceedings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17A(3)(b) a Syariah Court divorce event follows the commencement of the civil proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `divorce proceedings commenced in the Syariah Court on`
        WHEN JUST d THEN d GREATER THAN p's `commenced in the General Division on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    OR  CONSIDER p's `decree or order for divorce made by the Syariah Court on`
        WHEN JUST d THEN d GREATER THAN p's `commenced in the General Division on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    OR  CONSIDER p's `divorce registered under section 102 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 on`
        WHEN JUST d THEN `s 17A(3A) the registration of the divorce counts for section 17A(3)` d EQUALS JUST TRUE AND d GREATER THAN p's `commenced in the General Division on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 17A(3) as a regulative rule (ruling N2: derived from the decision above). The bearer is "the General Division"; the section sets no time for the stay.
DECLARE `s 17A(3) party` IS ONE OF `s 17A(3) the General Division`
DECLARE `s 17A(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 17A(3) stays the civil proceedings`
    `s 17A(3) takes some other step in the civil proceedings`

@ref s 17A(3) the General Division is to stay the civil proceedings (src:1137-1141)
GIVEN p IS A `s 17A civil proceedings`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 17A(3) party` `s 17A(3) act`
`s 17A(3) the General Division must stay the civil proceedings` MEANS
    IF `s 17A(3) the General Division is to stay the civil proceedings` p EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `s 17A(3) the General Division`
         MUST `s 17A(3) stays the civil proceedings`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 17A(3): the General Division is to stay the civil proceedings"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 17A(3A). A registered divorce counts under s 17A(3) only if registered before 1 March 2009 (the core holds the date).
-- src:1165 | (3A) For the purposes of subsection (3), any reference to the
-- src:1166 | registration of any divorce, or to a divorce that is registered, under
-- src:1167 | section 102 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 is to be
-- src:1168 | construed as a reference to the registration of a divorce or to a divorce
-- src:1169 | that is registered under that section before 1 March 2009.
@ref s 17A(3A) (src:1165-1169)
GIVEN registered IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(3A) the registration of the divorce counts for section 17A(3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF registered LESS THAN `the day before which a registered Muslim divorce counts under s 17A(3A)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "registration of a divorce ... under that section before 1 March 2009"

-- s 17A(4). If the Syariah Court proceedings and the civil proceedings are commenced on the same day, the Syariah Court proceedings are deemed commenced first.
-- src:1173 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), where the proceedings in the
-- src:1174 | Syariah Court are commenced on the same day as the civil
-- src:1175 | proceedings in the General Division, the proceedings in the
-- src:1182 | Syariah Court are deemed to have been commenced before the civil
-- src:1183 | proceedings.
@ref s 17A(4) (src:1173-1183)
GIVEN `the civil proceedings are commenced on` IS A DATE
      `the proceedings in the Syariah Court are commenced on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(4) the Syariah Court proceedings are deemed to have been commenced before the civil proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings in the Syariah Court are commenced on` EQUALS `the civil proceedings are commenced on` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the proceedings in the Syariah Court are commenced on` LESS THAN `the civil proceedings are commenced on` THEN JUST TRUE -- commenced before in fact: the deeming adds nothing
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the proceedings in the Syariah Court are commenced on the same day"

-- s 17A(7). In exercising jurisdiction or powers under (2), the General Division applies the civil law.
-- src:1204 | (7) To avoid any doubt, the General Division, in exercising its
-- src:1205 | jurisdiction or powers under subsection (2), is to apply the civil law.
@ref s 17A(7) (src:1204-1205)
GIVEN `the General Division is exercising jurisdiction or powers under section 17A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division exercising jurisdiction or powers under section 17A(2) (maintenance, custody, or property on divorce)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(7) the General Division applies the civil law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the General Division is exercising jurisdiction or powers under section 17A(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in exercising its jurisdiction or powers under subsection (2)"

-- s 17A(8). Despite s 3(2) of the Women's Charter 1961, s 112 of that Act applies to the General Division in the exercise of jurisdiction or powers under (2)(c).
-- src:1209 | (8) Despite section 3(2) of the Women’s Charter 1961, section 112
-- src:1210 | of that Act applies to the General Division in the exercise of its
-- src:1211 | jurisdiction or powers under subsection (2)(c).
@ref s 17A(8) (src:1209-1211)
GIVEN subject IS A `Subject of the case` @desc What is the proceeding about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(8) section 112 of the Women's Charter 1961 applies to the General Division in the proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `disposition or division of property on divorce` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the exercise of its jurisdiction or powers under subsection (2)(c)"

-- s 17A(9). The three terms. The Syariah Court is the court constituted under the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966; the two certificates are issued under s 35A(4) of that Act.
-- src:1215 | (9) In this section —
-- src:1217 | “Syariah Court” means the Syariah Court constituted under the
-- src:1218 | Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966;
-- src:1220 | “Syariah Court commencement certificate” means a
-- src:1221 | commencement certificate issued by the Syariah Court
-- src:1222 | under section 35A(4) of the Administration of Muslim Law
-- src:1223 | Act 1966;
-- src:1225 | “Syariah Court continuation certificate” means a continuation
-- src:1226 | certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4)
-- src:1227 | of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966.
@ref s 17A(9) “Syariah Court” (src:1215-1227)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(9) Syariah Court: the court is the Syariah Court constituted under the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Syariah Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Syariah Court” means the Syariah Court constituted under the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966"

@ref s 17A(9) “Syariah Court commencement certificate” (src:1220-1223)
GIVEN `it is a commencement certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a commencement certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(9) Syariah Court commencement certificate: it is a commencement certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4)` MEANS
    JUST `it is a commencement certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966`

@ref s 17A(9) “Syariah Court continuation certificate” (src:1225-1227)
GIVEN `it is a continuation certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a continuation certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17A(9) Syariah Court continuation certificate: it is a continuation certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4)` MEANS
    JUST `it is a continuation certificate issued by the Syariah Court under section 35A(4) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966`

§§§ `Sections 16, 17 and 17A together`

-- Gathering by hand (ruling E1, option B as guidance; fork F9). The sections give routes to one effect, "the General Division has civil jurisdiction": s 16(1), s 16(2), s 17(1), s 17A(2) are routes, and
-- s 17A(1) takes it away "despite sections 16 and 17". This calls each section's own answer, passed in; it restates no rule. A route that is JUST TRUE gives JUST TRUE; s 17A(1) JUST TRUE gives JUST FALSE;
-- otherwise the Act does not say (NOTHING).
@ref ss 16, 17 and 17A together (no single source line: a combination of the answers of ss 16(1), 16(2), 17(1), 17A(1) and 17A(2))
GIVEN `s 16(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 16(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 17(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 17A(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 17A(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 16, 17 and 17A the General Division has civil jurisdiction by one of these sections` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 17A(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite sections 16 and 17, the General Division has no jurisdiction"
        IF `s 16(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 16(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 17(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 17A(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the routes are listed without "only"; a case under none of them is not decided by these sections
